cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TariffTrail or the Calibrated Tree Descent pattern, please cite it as below."
title: "TariffTrail: calibrated tree descent with Strands Decider 2B for US tariff classification"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hiremath
    given-names: Mahantesh
    alias: mahanteshimath
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahanteshimath/AWS-Strands-Decider-Hackathon"
url: "https://main.d3o5ktn9yc15oj.amplifyapp.com/"
abstract: >-
  An agent that classifies products into 10-digit US HTS codes by walking the official tariff tree with Strands Decider 2B
  (best-first search on path probability), choosing among real candidate codes with one Amazon Bedrock call, and
  guarding the filing action with a Strands intervention handler. Includes a reusable single-file decision pattern.
keywords:
  - strands-decider
  - tariff-classification
  - harmonized-tariff-schedule
  - calibrated-decision-making
  - amazon-bedrock
  - ai-agents
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
